    "summary": "Female figure carved from wood [Ricinodendron africanum ?] with integral circular base. The figure has a diamond shaped face with narrow eyes. The top half of the face is pigmented with red (Ngula?) and the lower half with white. The upper body is also pigmented with red (Ngula?) while the lower half and base are covered with a layer of white pigment. The figure has a coiffure carved and dyed black which divides in two with a central band of braiding.",
